# Pairs with DedupNeverDropsNew. An apply that fails all the way to the
# dead-letter queue keeps its identity-cache reservation instead of rolling it
# back (ReplicationApplier's catch removes it). The operator's replay of the
# dead letter then hits the cache and is dropped as a duplicate of a write the
# receiver never applied.
MODULE: DedupNeverDropsNewFailedApplyKeepsReservation
TARGET: DedupNeverDropsNew
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: a dead-lettered apply keeps its identity reservation, so the operator's replay is dropped as a duplicate
PERTURBS: ApplyFails

--- FIND
       /\ dlq' = [dlq EXCEPT ![x] = @ \cup {w}]
       /\ cursor'
--- REPLACE
       /\ dlq' = [dlq EXCEPT ![x] = @ \cup {w}]
\* MUTATION: the reservation taken before the failed apply is not released.
       /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![x] = @ \cup {Ident(w)}]
       /\ cursor'
--- END

--- FIND
       /\ UNCHANGED <<authored, wal, val, pinned, cache, parking, buf, booted, skipped, requested>>
--- REPLACE
       /\ UNCHANGED <<authored, wal, val, pinned, parking, buf, booted, skipped, requested>>
--- END
